msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3202
msgctxt "orders-comms"
msgid "Visit lounge"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3203
msgctxt "orders-comms"
msgid ""
"When you enter the lounge, you see a guy sitting at the bar with an eye "
"patch, a peg leg, a cutlass at his belt, a three-cornered hat and a green "
"bird on his shoulder."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3204
msgctxt "orders-comms"
msgid "Ask about the eye patch, hat, peg leg and bird"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3205
#, lua-format
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Why, I'm a pirate, matey! Marcus the pirate! Actually, I'm just playing the "
"part of a pirate in the live production of 'Caribbean Pirates' here on %s. "
"I'm on a ten-minute rehearsal break. This stuff I'm wearing is my costume. "
"The peg leg is a hologram and the bird is a robot. I think the bird has "
"better lines than I do.\n"
"\n"
"If you want to talk to real modern pirates, that couple over there at that "
"table are the real deal. They recently retired from a successful career as "
"pirates, or so I hear. This will probably be the only time you can talk to "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3207
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "Talk to pirate couple"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3208
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Hi there, take a seat with us. Marcus signaled us that you've got some kind "
"of interest in pirates. Is that right?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3209
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "Yes, I want to know about pirates"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3210
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Well, we can tell you about it. Not that we would ever engage in such "
"practices ourselves."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3211
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "Of course. How would one get loot from another ship?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3212
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Loot?! We'd prefer to call that excess cargo. [they laugh at their own "
"joke]\n"
"\n"
"Several things have to come together in order to relieve them of their "
"excess cargo."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3213
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "What things have to come together?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3214
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Things your ship has to do and things that have to happen on the ship you're "
"liberating excess cargo from. Your ship has to be within 3 units of the "
"other ship, it has to be at a complete stop, it has to have the shields "
"down, it has to have room in the cargo bay, and it has to have at least 50 "
"units of energy per cargo item to operate the transporters that grab the "
"cargo."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3215
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "What about the other ship?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3216
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Assuming you haven't destroyed it (a common mistake with inexperienced "
"pirates), the other ship has to be completely immobile and their shields "
"have to be down. It also helps if they actually have excess cargo to "
"liberate."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3217
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "How do we know if they have any cargo?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3218
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Sometimes you can just ask them. Otherwise you can double scan them. You "
"should see the cargo manifest in the ship description. You may have to click "
"the tactical widget or the systems widget on the science console to see the "
"description."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3219
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "How do we get them to stop?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3220
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Your weapons officer can focus beams on their impulse engines. Once they're "
"in the negatives for their impulse engines, they won't be able to move. If "
"you've double scanned them, your science officer can check the status of "
"their impulse engines by clicking the tactical or description widget and "
"selecting systems.\n"
"\n"
"Now, some freighters have jump drives. You may need to disable those, too. "
"If you don't have beams, you have to use your missiles very carefully to "
"keep from destroying them altogether. You can't get cargo once they're "
"destroyed."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3221
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "How do we get their shields down?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3222
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"First, shoot them down, then target the applicable shield generator to keep "
"them down."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3223
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "Is that it?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3224
#, lua-format
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Once you meet all those requirements, your Relay or Operations officer "
"should see buttons to get cargo from the ship.\n"
"\n"
"Once you go down this path, there's no going back. If you stick to "
"liberating cargo from enemies of the %s, you'll only be called Licensed "
"Privateers. Loot neutrals or friendlies and you'll be labeled Pirates."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3225
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "What do we do with the excess cargo?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3226
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Sell it to stations that want to buy it. In fact, you should identify what "
"stations want what goods before you start liberating excess cargo from "
"innocent freighters."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3227
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "How do we find out what stations want goods?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3228
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Talk to them. Near the end of their status report, they'll say what goods "
"they sell and what goods they'll buy."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3229
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "Thanks for your help"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3230
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Don't mention it\n"
"\n"
"...to anyone...\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"   ---EVER---"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3242
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "No, I'm not interested in pirates"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/scenario_23_pirate.lua:3243
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "Suit yourself. Good luck."
msgstr ""

